From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 22:20:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(llama-cpp): the MoE cache starts from a record of the
 experts used

Carried as a llama.cpp patch beside the others
(patches/0017-moe-record.patch), after the parking prototype.

A mixture-of-experts model whose experts are kept in host memory
(`n_cpu_moe`, `moe_cache_mib`) keeps the experts it uses most in a GPU
cache. The cache's knowledge of which those are dies with its context, so
every load starts with an empty cache and uploads expert by expert under
its first tokens: the first answer after a load is the slow one.

With LLAMA_MOE_RECORD_DIR=<dir> in the model's environment the engine keeps
a record of the experts used - per layer and expert, decayed over a few
answers - in memory with the model and in a file of that directory. A cache
is filled from it when it is created, inside the load, the best-ranked
experts first and in runs; its eviction order is seeded from the same
record; when the cache goes, what it saw is folded in and the file written
(temporary name, then renamed). The record decides where an expert is read
from, never what is computed: with no share of the misses on the CPU the
outputs are the same with and without it. A file of other weights or of
another build, or one that cannot be read, is ignored with one log line.
The GPU memory of the cache does not change.

Unset: nothing is read or kept.

STAGED. The record's own test (tests/test-moe-record.cpp, standard library
only) passes; the fill compiles (g++, icpx 2025.3.3) and has not run where
it was written: it needs a GPU beside the host. On a device: one fixed
question at temperature 0, on a cache with no record, in a second context
of the same process and in a new process that reads the file - the load's
seconds, the time to the first token, the cache's own "hits, misses,
uploaded" lines, and the same token ids in all three.

Assisted-by: Claude Code
