 .../llama-cpp/patches/0017-moe-record.patch   | 790 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 790 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 backend/cpp/llama-cpp/patches/0017-moe-record.patch

diff --git a/backend/cpp/llama-cpp/patches/0017-moe-record.patch b/backend/cpp/llama-cpp/patches/0017-moe-record.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..dde9bc6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/backend/cpp/llama-cpp/patches/0017-moe-record.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,790 @@
+moe-cache: the experts used are recorded beyond a context, and a cache is filled from the record
+
+The MoE cache keeps the recently and repeatedly used experts of
+host-resident MoE layers in a device buffer. What it knows of which experts
+those are - a score of use per layer and expert - lives and dies with the
+context: every new context, and so every load, starts with an empty cache
+and fills it miss by miss, an upload at a time, under its first tokens.
+
+With LLAMA_MOE_RECORD_DIR=<dir> that knowledge is kept (llama-moe-record.h):
+per layer and expert, the lookups that selected the expert, decayed over
+4,096 tokens of its layer - answers, where the cache's own score decays over
+128 tokens.
+- when a cache is created (inside the context's creation, before any token)
+  it is FILLED from the record: the best-ranked experts of each group of
+  layers, as many as it has slots, uploaded in runs of consecutive experts;
+  one log line says how many, how many MiB and in how long;
+- the eviction order is seeded from the same record (moe_cache_lru::seed):
+  each expert put in gets the score its recorded use would have given it,
+  so what leaves first is what the record ranks last, and the real uses
+  take over as they come;
+- when the cache goes, what it saw is folded into the record - in memory
+  with the model (llama_model::moe_record), so the next context of the
+  process starts from it, and in a file of the directory, so the next
+  process does. The file is written whole under a temporary name and
+  renamed, never while the cache computes.
+
+The record only ever decides WHERE an expert is read from: an expert in the
+cache and an expert uploaded at a miss are the same bytes through the same
+kernels, so with no share of the misses on the CPU (--moe-cache-cpu-share 0,
+the default) the outputs are the same with and without it. With a CPU share
+the state of the cache already decides which kernels compute a miss; a
+cache that starts full applies that share from its first token.
+
+A file is used only by the weights and the build that wrote it (the
+model's name, sizes and shape, and a stamp compiled into the library, are
+in its name and in it): another model's, another build's, a cut or changed
+file is ignored with one log line and never a reason not to load. It holds
+counts, no text. The device memory of the cache does not change: its buffer
+is allocated whole when the cache is created, as before; the record decides
+what is in it.
+
+Unset: no record is read or kept, and the cache behaves as before.
+
+Tested: tests/test-moe-record.cpp (standard library only: the choice of
+experts, the decay, the file - every cut and every changed byte refused).
+The fill itself needs a second device: it compiles (g++, icpx 2025.3.3) and
+has not run where it was written.
